s in `CollaborativeEditing.js` in `external/sdkjs`, committed on its `pkt/PKT-0087` branch. When the code gathers the objects touched by a remote batch, a \"new object registered\" change now stands in for the object it registers (`NewClass`, or looked up by its `Id`).\n- If neither gives an object, it falls back to the full walk.\n- If the registered object isn't a run or paragraph-type element, it also falls back. So the collected fonts still include everything the full walk would find.\n- `Paragraph` is already accepted (it inherits `CDocumentContentElementBase`), so `Document.js` needed no change.\n\n**Acceptance:**\n- `sdkjs-word.sh`: 42/42 suites passed, 6195 assertions.\n- `unit.sh`: 178 passed, 1 skipped.\n- `theseus validate`: 0 errors, 1 warning.\n\n**Not done:** the packet asks for the A/B timing recipe in `baseline.md` to be re-run, but `baseline.md` is outside this packet's target files. I recorded a follow-up request in `.theseus/spawn/` to re-run it after this change, expecting 30/30 remote batches on the incremental path and about 140 ms saved per 30 changes. The follow-up's acceptance only checks that `baseline.md` mentions PKT-0087, so it won't verify the measured numbers.\n\nThe executor log, a friction line and the follow-up request are committed on the packet branch.\n\n**Lesson for the Atlas:** a remote batch that creates objects includes \"new object registered\" changes whose class is the object registry itself (`g_oTableId`). Any code that works per object over applied changes has to look through them to the new object (`NewClass`).","ttft_ms":1886,"type":"result","duration_ms":164288,"uuid":"783731f1-645a-4226-beeb-63bd88d8e8c9","ttft_stream_ms":939,"time_to_request_ms":351,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":4,"system_prompt":255,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":15,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":11,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":5,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_en